    },
    {
      "block_id": 11,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "## 8",
      "source_line": 24,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 12,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "## INTRODUCTION TO TRIGONOMETRY",
      "source_line": 26,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 13,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Trigonometry is the study of relationships between the sides and angles of a triangle.",
      "source_line": 28,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 14,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "### 11.2 Trigonometric Ratios",
      "source_line": 30,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 15,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "To know the trigonometric ratio we have to consider right angle triangle.",
      "source_line": 32,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 16,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "![Diagram showing two right-angled triangles, labeled 1 and 2, illustrating the sides (Opposite, Adjacent, Hypotenuse) relative to an angle A.](8c378a184b5ae4d1605cb74d7b7a7e3f_img.jpg)",
      "source_line": 34,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 17,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Diagram showing two right-angled triangles, labeled 1 and 2, illustrating the sides (Opposite, Adjacent, Hypotenuse) relative to an angle A.",
      "source_line": 36,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 18,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "| Trigonometric ratios |                        | 1               | 2               |\n|----------------------|------------------------|-----------------|-----------------|\n| SinA                 | Opposite<br>Hypotenuse | $\\frac{BC}{AC}$ | $\\frac{AB}{AC}$ |\n| CosA                 | Adjacent<br>Hypotenuse | $\\frac{AB}{AC}$ | $\\frac{BC}{AB}$ |\n| Tan A                | Opposite<br>Adjacent   | $\\frac{BC}{AB}$ | $\\frac{AB}{BC}$ |\n| CosecA               | Hypotenuse<br>Opposite | $\\frac{AC}{BC}$ | $\\frac{AC}{AB}$ |\n| SecA                 | Hypotenuse<br>Adjacent | $\\frac{AC}{AB}$ | $\\frac{AC}{BC}$ |\n| CotA                 | Adjacent<br>Opposite   | $\\frac{AB}{BC}$ | $\\frac{BC}{AB}$ |",
      "source_line": 38,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 19,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "**There are six trigonometric ratios:**",
      "source_line": 47,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 20,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "**Example 1:**  $\\tan A = \\frac{4}{3}$  find the other trigonometric ratios",
      "source_line": 49,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 21,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "of the angle A",
      "source_line": 51,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 22,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "In  $\\triangle ABC$ ,  $\\angle ABC = 90^\\circ$",
      "source_line": 53,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 23,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "$\\therefore$  By Pythagoras theorem,",
      "source_line": 55,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 24,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$AC^2 = AB^2 + BC^2$$",
      "source_line": 57,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 25,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow AC^2 = 4^2 + 3^2 = 16 + 9 = 25$$",
      "source_line": 59,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 26,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow AC = 5$$",
      "source_line": 61,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 27,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\sin A = \\frac{BC}{AC} = \\frac{4}{5}, \\cos A = \\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{3}{5}, \\tan A = \\frac{BC}{AB} = \\frac{4}{3}$$",
      "source_line": 63,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 28,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\csc A = \\frac{AC}{BC} = \\frac{5}{4}, \\sec A = \\frac{AC}{AB} = \\frac{5}{3}, \\cot A = \\frac{AB}{BC} = \\frac{3}{4}$$",
      "source_line": 65,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 29,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "![Diagram of a right-angled triangle ABC, right-angled at B. Side AB = 3, BC = 4, and AC = 5.](df9ce5affceb4ff1e9e8fd8e3ff0c1bd_img.jpg)",
      "source_line": 67,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 30,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Diagram of a right-angled triangle ABC, right-angled at B. Side AB = 3, BC = 4, and AC = 5.",
      "source_line": 69,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 31,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "**Example 2:** If B and Q are acute angles such that  $\\sin B = \\sin Q$ , then prove that  $\\angle B = \\angle Q$ .",
      "source_line": 71,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 32,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\sin B = \\sin Q$$",
      "source_line": 73,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 33,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{AC}{AB} = \\frac{PR}{PQ}$$",
      "source_line": 75,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 34,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{AC}{PR} = \\frac{AB}{PQ} = k \\quad \\text{--- (1)}$$",
      "source_line": 77,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 35,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$BC = \\sqrt{AB^2 - AC^2} \\text{ [By Pythagoras theorem]}$$",
      "source_line": 79,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 36,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow \\sqrt{k^2 PQ^2 - k^2 PR^2}$$",
      "source_line": 81,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 37,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow k \\sqrt{PQ^2 - PR^2} \\text{ [from (1)]}$$",
      "source_line": 83,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 38,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$QR = \\sqrt{PQ^2 - PR^2}$$",
      "source_line": 85,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 39,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{BC}{QR} = \\frac{k \\sqrt{PQ^2 - PR^2}}{\\sqrt{PQ^2 - PR^2}} = k \\quad \\text{--- (2)}$$",
      "source_line": 87,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 40,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "From (1) and (2),",
      "source_line": 89,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 41,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "![Diagram showing two right-angled triangles, BAC and QPR, right-angled at C and R respectively. Angle B is equal to angle Q.](6897c6cc242ac1382625f2128dcbe322_img.jpg)",
      "source_line": 91,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 42,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Diagram showing two right-angled triangles, BAC and QPR, right-angled at C and R respectively. Angle B is equal to angle Q.",
      "source_line": 93,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 43,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\frac{AC}{PR} = \\frac{AB}{PQ} = \\frac{BC}{QR}$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle PQR$$\n$$\\therefore \\angle B = \\angle Q$$",
      "source_line": 95,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 44,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "**Example 3 :** Consider  $\\triangle ACB$ , right-angled at C, in which  $AB = 29$  units,  $BC = 21$  units and  $\\angle ABC = \\theta$  (see Fig. 8.10). Determine the values of  $\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta$  (ii)  $\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$",
      "source_line": 99,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 45,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "In right angle triangle  $ACB$ ,  $\\angle ACB = 90^\\circ$",
      "source_line": 101,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 46,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\text{Therefore } AC = \\sqrt{AB^2 - BC^2}$$",
      "source_line": 103,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 47,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow AC = \\sqrt{29^2 - 21^2}$$",
      "source_line": 105,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 48,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow AC = \\sqrt{841 - 441} = \\sqrt{400} = 20$$",
      "source_line": 107,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 49,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\text{(i) } \\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta = \\frac{21^2}{29^2} + \\frac{20^2}{29^2} = \\frac{441+400}{841} = \\frac{841}{841} = 1$$",
      "source_line": 109,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 50,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\text{(ii) } \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta = \\frac{21^2}{29^2} - \\frac{20^2}{29^2} = \\frac{441-400}{841} = \\frac{41}{841} = 1$$",
      "source_line": 111,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 51,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "![Figure 8.10: A right-angled triangle ACB, right-angled at C. The hypotenuse AB is 29 units. The side BC is 21 units. The angle ABC is theta.](b48d146cf1d6e0a01791f52572be6767_img.jpg)",
      "source_line": 113,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 52,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Figure 8.10: A right-angled triangle ACB, right-angled at C. The hypotenuse AB is 29 units. The side BC is 21 units. The angle ABC is theta.",
      "source_line": 115,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 53,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Fig. 8.10",
      "source_line": 117,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 54,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "**Example 4 :** In a right triangle  $ABC$ , right-angled at B, if  $\\tan A = 1$ , then verify that  $2\\sin A \\cos A = 1$",
      "source_line": 119,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 55,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "In right angle triangle  $ACB$ ,",
      "source_line": 121,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 56,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\tan A = 1 \\Rightarrow \\frac{AB}{BC} = 1$$",
      "source_line": 123,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 57,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow AB = BC$$",
      "source_line": 125,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 58,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$AC^2 = AB^2 + BC^2 \\text{ [By Pythagoras theorem]}$$",
      "source_line": 127,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 59,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow AC^2 = 2AB^2 \\quad \\text{--- (1)}$$",
      "source_line": 129,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 60,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\text{Now, } 2\\sin A \\cos A = 2 \\cdot \\frac{AB}{AC} \\cdot \\frac{BC}{AC}$$",
      "source_line": 131,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 61,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$= 2 \\cdot \\frac{AB^2}{AC^2}$$",
      "source_line": 133,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 62,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$= 2 \\cdot \\frac{AB^2}{2AB^2} = 1$$",
      "source_line": 135,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 63,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "![Figure 8.11: A right-angled triangle ABC, right-angled at B. Angle A is shown.](090b77852b0817ee9fa4c9676aa027e4_img.jpg)",
      "source_line": 137,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 64,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Figure 8.11: A right-angled triangle ABC, right-angled at B. Angle A is shown.",
      "source_line": 139,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 65,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "Fig. 8.11",
      "source_line": 141,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 66,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "verbatim_content": "**Example 5 :** In  $\\triangle OPQ$  right-angled at P,  $OP = 7$  cm and  $OQ - PQ = 1$  cm (see Fig. 11.12). Determine the values of  $\\sin Q$  and  $\\cos Q$ .",
      "source_line": 143,
      "has_inline_latex": true
    },
    {
      "block_id": 67,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\text{In } \\triangle OPQ, OQ^2 = PQ^2 + OP^2 \\text{ [By Pythagoras theorem]}$$",
      "source_line": 145,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 68,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow (1 + PQ)^2 = PQ^2 + 7^2$$",
      "source_line": 147,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 69,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow 1 + PQ^2 + 2PQ = PQ^2 + 49$$",
      "source_line": 149,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 70,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow 1 + 2PQ = 49$$",
      "source_line": 151,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 71,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow 2PQ = 49 - 1 = 48$$",
      "source_line": 153,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 72,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow PQ = 24 \\text{ cm}$$",
      "source_line": 155,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 73,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow OQ = 1 + PQ = 1 + 24$$",
      "source_line": 157,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 74,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\Rightarrow OQ = 25$$",
      "source_line": 159,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 75,
      "block_type": "formula",
      "verbatim_content": "$$\\therefore \\sin Q = \\frac{7}{25} \\text{ and } \\cos Q = \\frac{24}{25}$$",
      "source_line": 161,
      "has_inline_latex": false
    },
    {
      "block_id": 76,
